{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 49, :comments ["<b>Your servants have taken the count of the men of war who are under our hand.</b> Under our authority. <b>And there lacked not one man of us.</b> This was a mighty wonder, among the great miracles that befell Israel, that befell them here in the war against Midian: for they were a multitude like the sand upon the seashore, and Israel slew of them and took captive of them thousands and tens of thousands, and Scripture testifies that not a single one of Israel was missing in the war. This is what it says: ולא נפקד ממנו איש. And this great miracle was because they were whole in merit — and this is what the Sages, of blessed memory, expounded: ולא נפקד ממנו איש — for matter of transgression. Moses said to them: If so, why this offering? They said: To atone for us for the musings of the heart."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:37:26.878892783Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}